# Memory-survival profile for the 1-GiB Prisma Compute instance class
# (OOM review, 2026-08-07). MEMORY knobs only — topology
# (INITIAL_SHARDS, FLEET_*) stays with each campaign's script.
#
# Every active deploy script sources this file and passes each line as
# --env; opting out requires UNSAFE_LEGACY_MEMORY_PROFILE=1
# explicitly. Values must be space-free (they are split into flags).
#
# The binary independently floors ABSORB_GLOBAL_BUDGET_BYTES at the
# worst-frame transient ((32 MiB frame + 64 KiB encoding allowance) x3
# build multiplier ≈ 96 MiB), and EVERY gather reserves at least that
# floor. At this budget EVERY gather — not just oversized ones — runs
# ONE AT A TIME (arm X survived at exactly that effective
# concurrency), so the slot count below is set to the effective truth.
# On larger instances set the budget to ~2x the floor (e.g. 201719808)
# AND ABSORB_GLOBAL_GATHERS=2 for two-way gathers. The startup summary
# prints both configured slots and EFFECTIVE concurrency.
ABSORB_GATHER_MAX_BYTES=8388608
ABSORB_GLOBAL_BUDGET_BYTES=100859904
ABSORB_GLOBAL_GATHERS=1
SLATEDB_RT_THREADS=4
TELEMETRY_CACHE_BYTES=16777216
SHARED_CACHE_BYTES=134217728
HISTORY_CACHE_BYTES=33554432
POSTINGS_CACHE_BYTES=67108864
MAX_UNFLUSHED_BYTES=16777216
L0_SST_SIZE_BYTES=8388608
L0_MAX_SSTS=32
ADMIT_RSS_SHED_MB=500
